---

<BaseLayout title={`Resume | ${SITE.title}`} sideBarActiveItemID="about">
  <script
    slot="head"
    type="application/ld+json"
    is:inline
    set:html={JSON.stringify(personSchema)}
  />
  <!-- Profile -->
  <section class="mb-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">About Me</h1>
    <p class="text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed text-justify">
      I'm a quantitative researcher and PhD candidate in Business Analytics & Operations
      Management at Sabanci University. My research applies reinforcement learning to
      quantitative finance problems: optimal trading, optimal execution, and portfolio
      optimisation. I also study market-regime learning and financial-market simulation, and
      build automated algorithmic trading strategies.
    </p>
    <p class="text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed text-justify mt-3">
      With an MSc in Business Analytics from the University of Edinburgh, I also work as a
      business analyst: turning multi-source data into automated pipelines, dashboards, and
      decision-ready analysis.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- Research -->
  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Research</h2>
    <h3 class="font-bold text-lg">Recurrent PPO for Optimal Trading of Bitcoin Perpetual Futures</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50 mb-3">PhD thesis, chapter one</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-base-content/75 leading-relaxed text-justify">
      A recurrent PPO agent (LSTM actor and critic) chooses a short, flat, or long position every
      hour in BitMEX XBTUSD perpetual futures, observing the market over horizons from one hour to
      one year and rewarded with the differential Sharpe ratio. It is retrained every year and
      evaluated on the following year in an expanding walk-forward design (2021 to August 2026),
      averaged over ten random initialisations.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-base-content/75 text-justify list-disc pl-4 marker:text-primary/40">
      <li>
        In the frictionless baseline, the agent reached a 89.7% CAGR and a 1.39 Sharpe ratio,
        against 14.8% and 0.53 for buy and hold and 33.5% and 0.78 for time-series momentum, the
        strongest benchmark, and was profitable in every test year on average.
      </li>
      <li>
        The baseline excludes fees, slippage, and funding payments; a realistic cost setup is in
        progress and portfolio-level work follows.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- Projects -->
  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Projects / Startups</h2>
    <div class="space-y-8">
      <div class="relative pl-6 border-l-2 border-primary/30">
        <div class="absolute -left-[7px] top-1.5 w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-primary"></div>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:justify-between sm:items-start gap-1">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-lg">
              <a href="https://portafel.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:text-primary transition-colors">Portafel &mdash; Financial Research Platform</a>
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/60">Founder</p>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50 sm:text-right shrink-0">Jan 2026 &mdash; Present</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-base-content/75 text-justify list-disc pl-4 marker:text-primary/40">
          <li>Financial-market research platform covering 10,987 active instruments across six asset classes: US-listed stocks, ETFs, world indices, commodities, FX pairs, and cryptocurrencies</li>
          <li>Consolidates company research (quotes and charts, financial statements, SEC filings, analyst estimates, news) with multi-factor stock screening and FinBERT news sentiment</li>
          <li>Private portfolios and watchlists with deterministic, evidence-linked alerts; web application with companion iOS and Android clients</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="relative pl-6 border-l-2 border-primary/30">
        <div class="absolute -left-[7px] top-1.5 w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-primary"></div>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:justify-between sm:items-start gap-1">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-lg">
              <a href="https://polymarket.mrzeynalli.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:text-primary transition-colors">Polymarket BTC 15-minute Backtesting Environment</a>
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/60">Independent project</p>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50 sm:text-right shrink-0">2026</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-base-content/75 text-justify list-disc pl-4 marker:text-primary/40">
          <li>Records the full public Level-2 order book, trades, and Binance and Chainlink BTC reference prices for BTC 15-minute Up/Down markets, normalised into versioned Parquet</li>
          <li>Deterministic simulator in which orders walk the actual price ladder, with partial fills, fees, latency, stale-book checks, and displayed-liquidity haircuts</li>
          <li>Indexes 570 markets recorded between 31 July and 6 August 2026, of which 285 meet strict backtesting requirements</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="relative pl-6 border-l-2 border-base-300">
        <div class="absolute -left-[7px] top-1.5 w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-base-300"></div>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:justify-between sm:items-start gap-1">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg">
            <a href="/blog/uk-cities-high-tech-potential" class="hover:text-primary transition-colors">Non-capital UK Cities with High-tech Potential</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50 sm:text-right shrink-0">Jan 2023</p>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/75 text-justify">
          Scraped Companies House records via API, filtered by SIC code, and ranked non-capital UK cities by tech-firm density and growth.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="relative pl-6 border-l-2 border-base-300">
        <div class="absolute -left-[7px] top-1.5 w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-base-300"></div>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:justify-between sm:items-start gap-1">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg">
            <a href="/blog/scottish_schools_clustering" class="hover:text-primary transition-colors">Scottish State Schools: K-Means Clustering</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50 sm:text-right shrink-0">Oct 2023</p>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/75 text-justify">
          Clustered 2,431 Scottish state schools by pupil count and SIMD deprivation score to identify local authorities needing NGO support; k=3 selected via WCSS and silhouette analysis.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- Education -->
  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Education</h2>
    <div class="space-y-8">
      {
        education.map(e => (
          <div class="relative pl-6 border-l-2 border-primary/30">
            <div class={`absolute -left-[7px] top-1.5 w-3 h-3 rounded-full ${e.primary ? "bg-primary" : "bg-base-300"}`} />
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:justify-between sm:items-start gap-1">
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-bold text-lg">{e.title}</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-base-content/60">{e.org}</p>
              </div>
              <div class="sm:text-right shrink-0">
                <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50">{e.dates}</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50">{e.place}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            {e.lines?.map(l => <p class="text-sm mt-2 text-base-content/70">{l}</p>)}
            {e.scholarship && <p class="text-xs mt-1 text-primary/70">{e.scholarship}</p>}
            {
              e.coursework && (
                <>
                  <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-base-content/40 mt-3 mb-1">Coursework</p>
                  <p class="text-sm text-base-content/60 text-justify">{e.coursework}</p>
                </>
              )
            }
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- Experience -->
  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Experience</h2>
    <div class="space-y-8">
      {
        experience.map(e => (
          <div class="relative pl-6 border-l-2 border-primary/30">
            <div class={`absolute -left-[7px] top-1.5 w-3 h-3 rounded-full ${e.primary ? "bg-primary" : "bg-base-300"}`} />
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:justify-between sm:items-start gap-1">
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-bold text-lg">{e.title}</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-base-content/60">{e.org}</p>
              </div>
              <div class="sm:text-right shrink-0">
                <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50">{e.dates}</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50">{e.place}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-base-content/75 text-justify list-disc pl-4 marker:text-primary/40">
              {e.lines?.map(l => <li>{l}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- Skills -->
  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Skills</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      {
        skills.map(group => (
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-base-content/50 uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">{group.heading}</h3>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              {group.items.map(item => <span class="badge badge-outline">{item}</span>)}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- Languages -->
  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Languages</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      {
        languages.map(l => (
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between p-3 rounded-lg bg-base-200/50">
            <span class="font-medium">{l.name}</span>
            <span class={`badge badge-sm ${l.primary ? "badge-primary" : "badge-ghost"}`}>{l.level}</span>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- Hobbies -->
  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Hobbies & Interests</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      {hobbies.map(h => <span class="badge badge-lg badge-ghost">{h}</span>)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <div class="text-center py-6">
    <a href="/projects" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">View My Projects</a>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
